# router-rebuild — what never enters git
#
# Three categories, and the reasons differ. Read the reason before adding an
# exception: two of these are not tidiness, they are the difference between a
# publishable repository and one that redistributes somebody else's property or
# identifies one physical device.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Planning material. May address the author directly, may discuss career
#    positioning. Committed files may not. (Same rule as the upstream repo.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
plan/
archive/
# study/ is the same category: teaching notes written for the author and for
# whoever the author is explaining this to. They address people directly and
# they restate things other files own. Committed files may not do either.
study/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Vendor documentation and vendor binaries. Not ours to redistribute.
#    SOURCES.json records the URL and the sha256 so anyone can obtain the same
#    file; that is the substitute for shipping it.
#    refs/README.md IS committed — it says what should be in refs/ and why the
#    directory is empty in a fresh clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
refs/*
!refs/README.md
*.pdf
*.web
*.bin
*.img

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Per-unit artefacts. A flash dump contains this unit's MAC addresses and
#    radio calibration; it identifies one physical device, not a model.
#    Binaries live in $FWRE_WORK (ext4, inside WSL) — never here, never under
#    /mnt/c. See plan/UPSTREAM-INVENTORY.md and the upstream
#    docs/workspace-layout.md for why that is a correctness rule and not a
#    performance one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dumps/*
!dumps/.gitkeep
!dumps/README.md
!dumps/MANIFEST.json
work/
extracted/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and toolchains
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
out/
staging/
toolchain/
# cloned GPL drops -- SOURCES.json says how to re-fetch each one.
# No trailing slash: on this machine src-vendor is a SYMLINK into ext4, not a
# directory, because NTFS is case-insensitive and the vendor kernel trees carry
# paths that differ only in case (xt_CONNMARK.h vs xt_connmark.h, and 29 more).
# A pattern ending in / matches directories only, and would have let the symlink
# itself be committed. tools/test-gitignore.sh case 14 is that check.
src-vendor
linux-*/
squashfs-root/
*.o
*.ko
*.a
*.so
*.squashfs
*.lzma
*.xz
vmlinux
System.map

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ghidra
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ghidra/decomp/
*.rep/
*.gpr
*.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
